# Toyota Prius XW20 five-door hatchback, 2004-2009.
#
# The second-generation Prius, the car that made the name a common sight in
# Britain. UK on sale 2 January 2004 at £17,495 for the T3, £18,295 for the T4
# and £19,995 for the T Spirit, on the road and excluding the £1,000 PowerShift
# grant; sold until 2009, when the XW30 replaced it.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Prius-gen2-UK-launch-pack-2003.pdf
# https://mag.toyota.co.uk/history-toyota-prius/
#
# Dimensions 4.450 x 1.725 x 1.490 m, wheelbase 2.700 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Prius (XW20)" infobox (NHW20). Mirrors take the modelled
# width to 1.961 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true side-elevation photograph of the XW20 was available
# when the car was built. The pack's image 1 is a shallow front-left
# three-quarter, and Wikimedia Commons was rate-limiting this machine on
# 2026-11-18 when a profile was sought. The flank was therefore built from the
# three-quarter photographs and the published dimensions, with the wheel
# centres set at the published wheelbase-to-length ratio of 60.7 per cent.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB brochure names, evidence grade (a): the 2005 and 2007
# UK brochures list Pure White, Decuma Grey, Vermillion Red, Verbier Green,
# Tyrol Silver, Astral Black, Aztec Bronze and Glacier Blue. Four common
# British finishes are modelled: Tyrol Silver, Pure White, Astral Black and
# Glacier Blue. Weights silver 3, white 3, black 2, blue 2, total 10,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h, the car's quoted maximum. Comfort 105/488, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 105: quiet and smooth, a step above the Corolla E120 and below
# the larger hybrid saloons. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 2004 intro, retires staggered 2016-2019 on a
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-prius-xw20.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-prius-xw20.dae (84 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-prius-xw20/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose and the rear bumper are squarer than the
# photographs, and the headlamp units do not sweep as far down into the front
# corners as the real car's. At 128 px the one-box arc, the high tail and the
# split hatch glass read as the second-generation Prius.

obj=citycar
